# --- s021 Book I d.3 q.6 (= Ord. I d.3 p.3 q.1, nn. 333–400: intelligible species)
n("n404","s021-01","Sexta questio tertie distinctionis","la","commentary","= *Ord.* I d. 3 p. 3 q. 1 (Vatican III, nn. 333–400). Scotus asks whether there is memory *habens speciem intelligibilem priorem naturaliter actu intelligendi*. Gorris drops the qualifier.","verified")
n("n405","s021-01","genitum assimilatur suo gignenti","la","source","The argument corresponds to *Ord.* I d. 3 n. 333 (first principal argument: the species, impressed by a singular, represents only a singular), answered at nn. 379–381.","verified")
n("n406","s021-02","opinio Henrici quodlibeto. 4°. q. 8.","la","source","Henry, *Quodl.* IV q. 8 (with V q. 14), against the intelligible species distinct from the act. The opinion is reported anonymously at *Ord.* I d. 3 nn. 340–345.","to-verify")
n("n407","s021-02","Ricardi maxime quodlibeto. 5°. q. 14","la","source","The identification is obscure. The *Quodl.* V q. 14 reference fits Henry, not Richard of Middleton (who left only three *Quodlibeta*). Possibly *Ricardi* is a compositor's error, or *maxime* belongs with Henry ('above all *Quodl.* V q. 14'). B to be checked.","uncertain")
n("n408","s021-02","Godofredus de fontibus quodlibeto. 9. q. 19.","la","source","*Ord.* I d. 3 n. 346: *Idem ponit alius doctor, negando speciem intelligibilem*. Godfrey of Fontaines, *Quodl.* IX q. 19 and XIII q. 3, is the standard identification (cf. n. 361, where Scotus's own addition names *Godefridus*).","certain")
n("n409","s021-02","huius intentionis sunt nominales","la","historical","A notable fifteenth-century gloss. Gorris aligns the deniers of the intelligible species (Henry, Godfrey) with the *nominales*, i.e. Ockham and his followers (*Rep.* II q. 12–13), who explain memory by habits. It reflects the *via antiqua / via moderna* polemics of the late fifteenth century. The point is repeated in ¶3 (*vt dicunt nominales*).","certain")
n("n410","s021-03","lapis non est in anima sed species lapidis","la","source","Arist. *De anima* III 8, 431b29–432a1, cited by Scotus at *Ord.* I d. 3 n. 344.","verified")
n("n411","s021-03","quatuor sunt species in anima altera ex altera nata","la","source","Aug. *De Trin.* XI 9.16: four species, *altera ex altera*, from the body to the sense, to memory, to the gaze of thought (*acies cogitantis*). Gorris's sequence (sense, phantasy, memory, act of understanding) adapts Augustine to the scholastic faculty psychology. The argument is not in *Ord.* I d. 3 p. 3 q. 1. Its source in the Scotist tradition is still to be identified.","to-verify")
n("n412","s021-03","noticia vespertina angelorum","la","source","The *cognitio matutina/vespertina* of the angels: Aug. *De Gen. ad litt.* IV 22–32. The arguments from angelic knowledge, from Christ's soul, from separated souls and from Paul's rapture (2 Cor. 12:2–4) are not in this question of the *Ordinatio*. They appear to be Gorris's or his school's additions.","to-verify")
n("n413","s021-03","illos non potuit habere in vnico actu","la","source","Arist. *Eth. Nic.* II 1, 1103a14–b25 (virtues and habits arise from repeated acts); cf. I 7, 1098a18 (*una hirundo non facit ver*).","certain")
n("n414","s021-04","causa particularis determinans causam vniuersalem","la","source","The doctrine of species and intellect as partial co-causes of intellection is Scotus's, in the next question of the *Ordinatio* (*Ord.* I d. 3 p. 3 q. 2, esp. nn. 496–500, *duae causae partiales*). Gorris anticipates it here.","certain")
n("n415","s021-05","ratio agendi est quidditas speciei. sed ecceitas est conditio ipsius","la","source","*Ord.* I d. 3 n. 380: *Singularitas est condicio agentis, non ratio agendi, sed ratio agendi est ipsa forma*. Gorris substitutes *ecceitas* for Scotus's *singularitas*, importing the vocabulary of *Ord.* II d. 3.","verified")
n("n416","s021-05","Ex predictis respondetur ad questionem","la","source","*Ord.* I d. 3 n. 370 (*Ad quaestionem ergo dico quod necesse est ponere in intellectu ut habet rationem memoriae, speciem intelligibilem…*).","verified")
n("n417","s021-02","The nominalists are of this mind","en","translation","Lit. ‘of this intention are the *nominales*’.","certain")
# --- B collation (full): B34L–B35L
upd("n407", append=" B: *Richardi maxime quoli. iij. q. xiiij.* (*iij* for A's *5°*; the numeral is clear in B).")
n("n1099","s021-02","Istud ponit doctor alius. iste alius est","la","textual","B: *Idem ponit doctor quidam. Iste quidam est*. B's *Idem* agrees with Scotus (*Ord.* I d. 3 n. 346: *Idem ponit alius doctor*).","certain")
upd("n415", append=" B misprints *ratio angeli* for *ratio agendi*.")
